        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(ui): Codex-style minimal sidebar — pinned/chats groups, icon footer, no brand header",
        "body": "Related: #100287\nStacked on #100296 (contains its commit; rebases to a single commit once that lands).\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nEven after #100296, the sidebar still carried chrome that competes with the conversation: a brand header row duplicating the topbar breadcrumb, a boxed RECENT header with its own collapse toggle, three pinned nav pages, and a stacked, labeled footer (Settings row, Docs row, status row, pair button). The feedback on #100296 was that the redesign did not go far enough.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis takes the sidebar to Codex-app minimalism. The brand header is gone — the sidebar starts with a quiet \"+ New session\" row. Sessions are the core content, split into tiny PINNED and CHATS sections (pinned rows surface automatically from the existing pin flag; the session-search picker sits inline next to the CHATS label). The RECENT collapse toggle and its persisted `recentSessionsCollapsed` setting are deleted outright. The default pinned nav shrinks to just Overview — everything else lives under More, and the right-click customize menu from #100296 still lets users pin whatever they want. The footer collapses to a single icon row: status dot left; Settings, Docs, and device-pairing icons right (theme toggle stays mobile-only). Net −192 lines of non-generated code while adding the session grouping.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThe default sidebar now shows: New session, your pinned chats, recent chats, All sessions, Overview, More — and a one-line footer. Chat gets the entire visual field. Session grouping (pinned vs chats) matches how the session list already behaves elsewhere, and upcoming session-threading work can slot into these groups without touching the nav model. Every removed affordance stays reachable: all pages under More or via customize, Settings/Docs as footer icons with tooltips, sidebar collapse from the topbar.\n\n## Evidence\n\nScreenshots (mocked-gateway e2e harness, dark, 1440×900) in the first PR comment: default state, More expanded, right-click customize menu.\n\n- Remote Testbox: 5 touched unit suites + sidebar session-management e2e (run IDs in PR comment).\n- Direct `tsgo -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.test.ui.json` clean.\n- `pnpm ui:i18n:sync` regenerated bundles for the new `nav.chats` string.\n- Codex autoreview on the v2 commit: result in PR comment.\n- `git diff --numstat`: −192 net non-generated LOC (deleted brand header, RECENT collapse plumbing, labeled footer rows, quota-era utility styles).\n",
